    "rationale": "The objective torch_communication.communication_kernel_sum_ms (baseline 94.49 ms; profiled reps 93.52/94.49/110.06) is produced exclusively by the 13 per-step NCCL AllReduce kernels dispatched through the two selected c10d::allreduce_ groups: 12 dispatches of 7,087,872 float32 elements (group f833b57a373d8262a384, call d0938de87369efd500322679) plus 1 dispatch of 39,385,344 elements (group 8525af72c631b94e3dd0, call b8ade439d7b8bd5fb5c1029b), together exactly the 497,759,232-byte FP32 gradient payload (resources.json cross_rank matched 13/13, incomplete empty; nsys shows exactly 13 NCCL kernels, all AllReduce on stream 17). Measured decomposition: isolated calibration of the identical ops (collective_calibration-1af5837f) gives 3.565/3.649 ms per small bucket and 19.49/19.64 ms for the large one, a per-rank transport floor of 62.3/63.4 ms that matches rank 1's in-step sum (63.66 ms) and the nsys rank-0 run (62.46 ms); the addressable excess is early-arrival waiting charged into kernel durations. execution_timeline-1221e205 localizes it: the FIRST collective (seq 21) ran 14.04 ms on rank 0 vs 3.62 ms on rank 1 (rank 0 launched ~10.5 ms early and both kernels ended within ~90 us), while every later kernel stayed at the transport floor on both ranks; the nsys run shows the same shape with the direction flipped (rank 1 first kernel 181.8 ms, rest at floor), so the remedy must be symmetric and per-call-independent. The previous candidate trial-92d5f02cbf on this exact joint boundary already validated the mechanism on the metric side: host-side SHM arrival alignment before dispatching the unchanged parent op measured 63.16-63.61 ms (the floor), bitwise-identical gradients (max_abs_error 0.0 over 248,879,621 compared elements) and full coverage (12+1 through context.references), but it applied the rendezvous at ALL 13 dispatches with a 100 us sleep-poll loop and 2 ms busy tail, and was rejected solely on the step_ms constraint: 240.5-251.9 ms on both ranks against the 151.86 ms limit (1.05x of the 144.63 ms baseline). The wall-time damage is explained by the rendezvous schedule, not the idea: after the first collective the NCCL stream is self-serializing at the ~3.6 ms transport cadence, so a per-dispatch host rendezvous makes every kernel's start hostage to the slower rank's HOST arrival (cadence above 3.6 ms), stretching the ~62 ms NCCL window to ~160 ms on both ranks. The two dispatch sites must remain one joint candidate because they share a single per-step arrival-state machine (whichever site fires first in the step performs the one alignment; both sites need the shared counter and parent references), and splitting them would leave the first-dispatch behavior undefined across bucket orders.",
    "hypothesis": "Repair of trial-92d5f02cbf on the same joint boundary: keep the symmetric cross-rank arrival alignment over the /dev/shm 8-byte counter page, but perform it exactly ONCE per accumulated step, at the FIRST c10d::allreduce_ dispatch (counting dispatches across both replaced sites; the first is always a 7,087,872-element bucket since the 39,385,344-element bucket dispatches last in the reducer's reverse order), and dispatch dispatches 2..13 straight to the unchanged parent op with no host wait. Replace the 100 us sleep-poll loop and 2 ms busy tail with a tight spin on the peer counter (bounded by a single budget parameter with graceful degrade: budget expiry or unreachable page falls back to the pure parent path, preserving baseline behavior and routes). Expected effect on the objective: the first kernel's in-device spin (~10.5 ms clean; 31-48 ms under the torch_communication collector, consistent with baseline reps 93.5/94.5/110.1 = floor + wait) is moved off the NCCL kernel, whose measured duration then falls to the transport floor; later kernels are already at floor in every observation, so the max-rank sum should land at ~62.3-63.6 ms (the previous trial empirically reached 63.16-63.61 with this alignment), a ~33% reduction from 94.49 ms. Expected effect on the constrained step_ms: the first kernel ENDS when the peer joins regardless of whether the wait spins on device or on the host, so the NCCL chain completion time is unchanged; the single ~10.5 ms clean-run host stall occurs while the GPU still holds ~20 ms of queued backward compute and the ~62 ms NCCL window is just beginning, so the CPU re-enqueues remaining backward and the optimizer long before either stream drains, keeping clean step_ms near the 144.63 ms baseline well inside the 151.86 ms limit; only ONE rendezvous per step removes the repeated host-cadence serialization that cost the previous trial ~100 ms on both ranks. This wall-time reasoning and the floor-level objective are hypotheses to be tested: the previous measurements establish feasibility of the metric floor and bitwise quality (unchanged parent op, same buckets, same process group), not wall-time safety of the single rendezvous, so the budget parameter bounds worst-case wall impact by degrading to the baseline parent path."
